      "id": "1bal6yc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. List of Fundamental Rights"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental Rights are covered under Part III of the Constitution spanning Articles 12 to 35.",
        "Articles 14 to 18 guarantee the Right to Equality, including non-discrimination and equality of opportunity.",
        "Articles 19 to 22 deal with the Right to Freedom, subject to reasonable restrictions.",
        "Articles 32 to 35 empower citizens to approach courts directly via Constitutional Remedies and Writs."
      ],
      "id": "rwy1enb"
    },
